IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-2-explanations`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`
IMPORT `chapter-4a-private-defence`

§ `Chapter 12 -- Offences relating to government stamps`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 255, 256, 257, 258, 259, 260, 261, 262, 263.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.
--
-- The nine live sections of a Chapter that once held thirty-five; the coin offences
-- were repealed in 2019 and replaced by ss 489A to 489I. What remains is the
-- revenue stamp, and the sections mirror the currency group: counterfeiting it
-- (s 255), the instruments and materials for doing so (ss 256, 257), selling,
-- possessing and using a counterfeit (ss 258 to 260), and three offences on GENUINE
-- stamps that have already been used -- effacing the writing so the stamp can be
-- reused (s 261), reusing a stamp (s 262), and erasing the mark that shows it used
-- (s 263).
--
-- s 255(2) makes "stamp" include a stamp certificate under the Stamp Duties Act 1929
-- for ss 255 to 262 but not s 263; so the revenue stamp and the certificate are two
-- facts, gathered by one rule for ss 255 to 262, and s 263 tests the first alone. The
-- s 255 Explanation -- making a genuine stamp of one denomination look like one of
-- another is counterfeiting -- is a second route into the s 255 act.
--
-- ss 261 to 263 open "fraudulently or with intent to cause loss to the Government".
-- "Fraudulently" is the s 25 term and comes from the Fault record; the intent to
-- cause loss is a fact on this one. Either suffices.
--
-- PUNISHMENT IS NOT COMPUTED.

§§ `Section 255(2) -- What the stamp is`

-- A stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue; and, for ss 255 to 262
-- only, a stamp certificate issued under the Stamp Duties Act 1929. s 263 is outside
-- the extension and tests the revenue stamp alone.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 255(2)"
GIVEN gs IS A `Government Stamp`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the stamp is a Government revenue stamp within sections 255 to 262` IF
        gs's `the stamp is a stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue`
    OR  gs's `the stamp is a stamp certificate issued under the Stamp Duties Act 1929`

§§ `Section 255 -- Counterfeiting a Government stamp`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 255 Explanation"
GIVEN gs IS A `Government Stamp`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person counterfeits the stamp` IF
        gs's `counterfeits or knowingly performs any part of the process of counterfeiting the stamp`
    OR  gs's `causes a genuine stamp of one denomination to appear like a genuine stamp of a different denomination`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 255"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes counterfeiting a Government stamp under Penal Code 1871 section 255
GIVEN gs IS A `Government Stamp` @desc Counterfeiting, or knowingly performing any part of the process of counterfeiting, a stamp issued by the Government for revenue (including a stamp certificate). Making one denomination look like another is counterfeiting.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes counterfeiting a Government stamp` IF
        `the stamp is a Government revenue stamp within sections 255 to 262` gs
    AND `the person counterfeits the stamp` gs

§§ `Sections 256 and 257 -- Instruments and materials for counterfeiting`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 256"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes possessing an instrument or material for counterfeiting a Government stamp under Penal Code 1871 section 256
GIVEN gs IS A `Government Stamp` @desc Possessing an instrument or material for the purpose of, or knowing or having reason to believe it is intended for, counterfeiting a Government revenue stamp.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes possessing instruments for counterfeiting a Government stamp` IF
        `the stamp is a Government revenue stamp within sections 255 to 262` gs
    AND gs's `has in his possession any instrument or material for the purpose of being used or knowing or having reason to believe that it is intended to be used for counterfeiting the stamp`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 257"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes making or selling an instrument for counterfeiting a Government stamp under Penal Code 1871 section 257
GIVEN gs IS A `Government Stamp` @desc Making, performing part of the making of, buying, selling or disposing of an instrument for the purpose of, or known or believed to be intended for, counterfeiting a Government revenue stamp.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes making or selling instruments for counterfeiting a Government stamp` IF
        `the stamp is a Government revenue stamp within sections 255 to 262` gs
    AND gs's `makes performs any part of the process of making buys sells or disposes of any instrument for the purpose of being used or knowing or having reason to believe that it is intended to be used for counterfeiting the stamp`

§§ `Sections 258 to 260 -- Selling, possessing and using a counterfeit stamp`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 258"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes sale of a counterfeit Government stamp under Penal Code 1871 section 258
GIVEN gs IS A `Government Stamp` @desc Selling or offering for sale a stamp known or believed to be a counterfeit of a Government revenue stamp.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes selling a counterfeit Government stamp` IF
        `the stamp is a Government revenue stamp within sections 255 to 262` gs
    AND gs's `sells or offers for sale a stamp which he knows or has reason to believe to be a counterfeit of the stamp`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 259"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes possession of a counterfeit Government stamp under Penal Code 1871 section 259
GIVEN gs IS A `Government Stamp` @desc Possessing a stamp known to be a counterfeit of a Government revenue stamp, intending to use or dispose of it as genuine or that it be so used.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes possessing a counterfeit Government stamp` IF
        `the stamp is a Government revenue stamp within sections 255 to 262` gs
    AND gs's `has in his possession a stamp which he knows to be a counterfeit of the stamp`
    AND gs's `intends to use or dispose of the counterfeit as a genuine stamp or in order that it may be used as a genuine stamp`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 260"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes using as genuine a Government stamp known to be counterfeit under Penal Code 1871 section 260
GIVEN gs IS A `Government Stamp` @desc Using as genuine a stamp known to be a counterfeit of a Government revenue stamp.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes using a counterfeit Government stamp` IF
        `the stamp is a Government revenue stamp within sections 255 to 262` gs
    AND gs's `uses as genuine a stamp knowing it to be a counterfeit of the stamp`

§§ `Sections 261 to 263 -- Reusing a genuine stamp`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 261 to 263"
GIVEN gs IS A `Government Stamp`
      f IS A Fault
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is fraudulent or intended to cause loss to the Government` gs f IF
        `the act is done fraudulently` f
    OR  gs's `intends to cause loss to the Government`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 261"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes effacing writing from a stamped substance or removing a used stamp with intent to cause loss to the Government under Penal Code 1871 section 261
GIVEN gs IS A `Government Stamp` @desc Fraudulently or intending loss to the Government, effacing from a stamped substance the writing the stamp was used for, or removing a used stamp from a writing, so the stamp may be used again.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements. Fraudulently is s 25.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes effacing writing or removing a used stamp` gs f IF
        `the act is fraudulent or intended to cause loss to the Government` gs f
    AND `the stamp is a Government revenue stamp within sections 255 to 262` gs
    AND gs's `removes or effaces from a substance bearing the stamp any writing or document for which the stamp has been used or removes from a writing or document a stamp which has been used for it in order that the stamp may be used for a different writing or document`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 262"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes using a Government stamp known to have been used before under Penal Code 1871 section 262
GIVEN gs IS A `Government Stamp` @desc Fraudulently or intending loss to the Government, using for any purpose a Government revenue stamp known to have been used before.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements. Fraudulently is s 25.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes reusing a Government stamp` gs f IF
        `the act is fraudulent or intended to cause loss to the Government` gs f
    AND `the stamp is a Government revenue stamp within sections 255 to 262` gs
    AND gs's `uses for any purpose the stamp which he knows to have been before used`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 263"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes erasing the mark denoting that a Government stamp has been used under Penal Code 1871 section 263
GIVEN gs IS A `Government Stamp` @desc Fraudulently or intending loss to the Government, erasing the mark that denotes a Government revenue stamp used, or knowingly possessing, selling or disposing of one from which the mark has been erased, or selling one known to have been used. s 255(2) does not extend "stamp" to a stamp certificate here.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements. Fraudulently is s 25.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes erasing the mark of a used Government stamp` gs f IF
        `the act is fraudulent or intended to cause loss to the Government` gs f
    AND gs's `the stamp is a stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue`
    AND gs's `erases or removes from the stamp a mark put or impressed on it to denote that it has been used or knowingly has in his possession or sells or disposes of a stamp from which such a mark has been erased or removed or sells or disposes of a stamp which he knows to have been used`

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes a counterfeit Government stamp offence` IF
        (   `constitutes counterfeiting a Government stamp` (a's `government stamp`)
         OR `constitutes possessing instruments for counterfeiting a Government stamp` (a's `government stamp`)
         OR `constitutes making or selling instruments for counterfeiting a Government stamp` (a's `government stamp`)
         OR `constitutes selling a counterfeit Government stamp` (a's `government stamp`)
         OR `constitutes possessing a counterfeit Government stamp` (a's `government stamp`)
         OR `constitutes using a counterfeit Government stamp` (a's `government stamp`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes a reused Government stamp offence` IF
        (   `constitutes effacing writing or removing a used stamp` (a's `government stamp`) (a's `fault`)
         OR `constitutes reusing a Government stamp` (a's `government stamp`) (a's `fault`)
         OR `constitutes erasing the mark of a used Government stamp` (a's `government stamp`) (a's `fault`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)
